#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:1
msgid "Release 2.32.0 (2025-10-06)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:3
msgid "Incompatible changes"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:5
msgid ""
"Removed support for daemons and clients older than Nix 2.0 [\\#13951]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13951)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:7
msgid ""
"We have dropped support in the daemon worker protocol for daemons and "
"clients that don't speak at least version 18 of the protocol. This first Nix "
"release that supports this version is Nix 2.0, released in February 2018."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:9
msgid ""
"Derivation JSON format now uses store path basenames only [\\#13570](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/13570) [\\#13980](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/13980)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:11
msgid ""
"Experience with many JSON frameworks (e.g. nlohmann/json in C++, Serde in "
"Rust, and Aeson in Haskell) has shown that the use of the store directory in "
"JSON formats is an impediment to systematic JSON formats, because it "
"requires the serializer/deserializer to take an extra parameter (the store "
"directory)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:13
msgid ""
"We ultimately want to rectify this issue with all JSON formats to the extent "
"allowed by our stability promises. To start with, we are changing the JSON "
"format for derivations because the `nix derivation` commands are — in "
"addition to being formally unstable — less widely used than other unstable "
"commands."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:15
msgid ""
"See the documentation on the [JSON format for derivations](../protocols/json/"
"derivation/index.md) for further details."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:17
msgid ""
"C API: `nix_get_attr_name_byidx`, `nix_get_attr_byidx` take a `nix_value *` "
"instead of `const nix_value *` [\\#13987](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/"
"13987)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:19
msgid ""
"In order to accommodate a more optimized internal representation of "
"attribute set merges these functions require a mutable `nix_value *` that "
"might be modified on access. This does _not_ break the ABI of these "
"functions."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:22
msgid "New features"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:24
msgid ""
"C API: Add lazy attribute and list item accessors [\\#14030](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/14030)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:26
msgid ""
"The C API now includes lazy accessor functions for retrieving values from "
"lists and attribute sets without forcing evaluation:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:28
msgid ""
"`nix_get_list_byidx_lazy()` - Get a list element without forcing its "
"evaluation"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:29
msgid ""
"`nix_get_attr_byname_lazy()` - Get an attribute value by name without "
"forcing evaluation"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:30
msgid ""
"`nix_get_attr_byidx_lazy()` - Get an attribute by index without forcing "
"evaluation"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:32
msgid ""
"These functions are useful when forwarding unevaluated sub-values to other "
"lists, attribute sets, or function calls. They allow more efficient handling "
"of Nix values by deferring evaluation until actually needed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:34
msgid ""
"Additionally, bounds checking has been improved for all `_byidx` functions "
"to properly validate indices before access, preventing potential out-of-"
"bounds errors."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:36
msgid ""
"The documentation for `NIX_ERR_KEY` error handling has also been clarified "
"to specify when this error code is returned."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:38
msgid "HTTP binary caches now support transparent compression for metadata"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:40
msgid ""
"HTTP binary cache stores can now compress `.narinfo`, `.ls`, and build log "
"files before uploading them, reducing bandwidth usage and storage "
"requirements. The compression is applied transparently using the `Content-"
"Encoding` header, allowing compatible clients to automatically decompress "
"the files."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:44
msgid "Three new configuration options control this behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:45
msgid "`narinfo-compression`: Compression method for `.narinfo` files"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:46
msgid "`ls-compression`: Compression method for `.ls` files"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:47
msgid ""
"`log-compression`: Compression method for build logs in `log/` directory"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:49
msgid "Example usage:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:50
msgid ""
"```\n"
"nix copy --to 'http://cache.example.com?narinfo-compression=gzip&ls-"
"compression=gzip' /nix/store/...\n"
"nix store copy-log --to 'http://cache.example.com?log-compression=br' /nix/"
"store/...\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:55
msgid ""
"Temporary build directories no longer include derivation names [\\#13839]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13839)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:57
msgid ""
"Temporary build directories created during derivation builds no longer "
"include the derivation name in their path to avoid build failures when the "
"derivation name is too long. This change ensures predictable prefix lengths "
"for build directories under `/nix/var/nix/builds`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:59
msgid ""
"External derivation builders [\\#14145](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/"
"14145)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:61
msgid ""
"These are helper programs that Nix calls to perform derivations for "
"specified system types, e.g. by using QEMU to emulate a different type of "
"platform. For more information, see the [`external-builders` setting](../"
"command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-external-builders)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:63
msgid "This is currently an experimental feature."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:65
msgid "Performance improvements"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:67
msgid ""
"Optimize memory usage of attribute set merges [\\#13987](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/13987)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:69
msgid ""
"[Attribute set update operations](../language/operators.md#update) have been "
"optimized to reduce reallocations in cases when the second operand is small."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:72
msgid ""
"For typical evaluations of nixpkgs this optimization leads to ~20% less "
"memory allocated in total without significantly affecting evaluation "
"performance."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:75
msgid ""
"See [eval-attrset-update-layer-rhs-threshold](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-eval-attrset-update-layer-rhs-threshold)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:77
msgid ""
"Substituted flake inputs are no longer re-copied to the store [\\#14041]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/14041)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:79
msgid ""
"Since 2.25, Nix would fail to store a cache entry for substituted flake "
"inputs, which in turn would cause them to be re-copied to the store on "
"initial evaluation. Caching these inputs results in a near doubling of "
"performance in some cases — especially on I/O-bound machines and when using "
"commands that fetch many inputs, like `nix flake [archive|prefetch-inputs]`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:81
msgid ""
"`nix flake check` now skips derivations that can be substituted [\\#13574]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13574)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:83
msgid ""
"Previously, `nix flake check` would evaluate and build/substitute all "
"derivations. Now, it will skip downloading derivations that can be "
"substituted. This can drastically decrease the time invocations take in "
"environments where checks may already be cached (like in CI)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:88
msgid "`fetchTarball` and `fetchurl` now correctly substitute (#14138)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:90
msgid ""
"At some point we stopped substituting calls to `fetchTarball` and `fetchurl` "
"with a set `narHash` to avoid incorrectly substituting things in "
"`fetchTree`, even though it would be safe to substitute when calling the "
"legacy `fetch{Tarball,url}`. This fixes that regression where it is safe."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:91
msgid ""
"Started moving AST allocations into a bump allocator [\\#14088](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/14088)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.32.md:93
msgid ""
"This leaves smaller, immutable structures in the AST. So far this saves "
"about 2% memory on a NixOS config evaluation."
msgstr ""

